cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the associated journal article and this archived repository."
type: software
title: "PVOS: Parallel Variation Operator Strategy research code"
abstract: >-
  Source code, experiment notebooks, consolidated post-analysis workbooks, and
  rendered figures for the Parallel Variation Operator Strategy (PVOS), a
  fixed-budget operator-level multi-crossover ensemble for multi-objective
  evolutionary optimization. The repository includes the PVOS-2C pairing study
  notebook (all six two-operator combinations), the baseline NSGA-II versus
  PVOS-4C notebook covering the 27-problem benchmark and the population-size
  sensitivity analysis, four adaptive operator-selection baselines (Borg, HNSGA,
  EnXEA, OVEA) instantiated over the common four-operator pool, host-transfer
  notebooks for SPEA2, NSGA-III, and AGE-MOEA2, the styrene monomer reactor
  case study for the single-bed, steam-injected, and double-bed configurations
  (process-model implementation, empirical reference sets, normalization
  bounds, and paired baseline NSGA-II and PVOS-4C notebooks), two Excel
  workbooks consolidating all main and supplementary tables, and the rendered
  manuscript figures. Per-run results and per-seed metrics are embedded in the
  executed notebooks. This is the public artifact referenced in the
  manuscript's Data availability statement.

